{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WA82qnE53YXnicLZ8b2cip","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\ngo-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The pipeline: extract behavior from C source, specify in SRDs, synthesize Go via mage-claude-orchestrator, verify with differential tests. 114 SRDs across 33 releases covering 111 utilities.\n\n**Implemented:** pkg/sys, pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil, and cmd/ utilities for sponge, du, true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, seq, wc, uname, arch, hostname, hostid. For cmd/ls, R1.1-R1.8 completed in tasks 5202/5203.\n\n**Current release:** rel04.0 (ls) is the earliest release with ready requirements. srd008-ls has 45 remaining ready requirements: R1.9-R1.14, R2.1-R2.15, R3.1-R3.15, R4.1-R4.9.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel04.0 is the earliest incomplete release with requirements in requirement_states. Earlier releases (00.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3, 02.0, 02.1, 02.2, 03.0, 03.1) either have all requirements complete or their SRDs are absent from requirement_states. Per P2, implementation and tests are split. Per P8, implementation before tests.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\nAll srd008-ls requirements assumed weight 1 (default):\n\n- Task 0: R1.9(1) + R1.10(1) + R1.11(1) + R1.12(1) = 4 ≤ 4\n- Task 1: R1.9(1) + R1.10(1) + R1.11(1) + R1.12(1) = 4 ≤ 4 (tests)\n- Task 2: R1.13(1) + R1.14(1) + R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) = 4 ≤ 4\n- Task 3: R1.13(1) + R1.14(1) + R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) = 4 ≤ 4 (tests)\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ls: core display features (srd008-ls R1.9-R1.12)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml (requirements R1.9, R1.10, R1.11, R1.12 -- read full text and acceptance criteria)\n      - cmd/ls/main.go (existing ls implementation covering R1.1-R1.8 -- extend this file)\n      - pkg/sys/ (FileInfo struct, Stat, Lstat for file metadata -- architecture dependency srd008-ls -> srd002-sys)\n      - pkg/format/ (HumanSize, PadLeft, PadRight, FileTypeColor, Columns -- architecture dependency srd008-ls -> srd003-format)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project build conventions and SIGPIPE handling requirement)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add implementation for srd008-ls requirements R1.9 through R1.12\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R1.9 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R1.10 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R1.11 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R1.12 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/sys.Stat and pkg/sys.Lstat for file metadata (mode, size, nlink, uid, gid, timestamps) per architecture dependency srd008-ls -> srd002-sys. Do not call syscall or golang.org/x/sys/unix directly from cmd/ls\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/format for output formatting (HumanSize, PadLeft, PadRight, FileTypeColor, Columns) per architecture dependency srd008-ls -> srd003-format. If pkg/format does not exist or is empty, implement the required formatting inline in cmd/ls/main.go\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Preserve sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() call at the start of main and all existing functionality from R1.1-R1.8 -- do not restructure existing code\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ls builds successfully with go build -o bin/ls ./cmd/ls/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"srd008-ls requirements R1.9, R1.10, R1.11, and R1.12 are fully implemented as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/ls/... passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Existing functionality from R1.1-R1.8 is preserved -- no regressions in flag parsing or output\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ls: core display features tests (srd008-ls R1.9-R1.12)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml (acceptance criteria for R1.9, R1.10, R1.11, R1.12 -- derive test inputs and expected behaviors from these)\n      - cmd/ls/main.go (current ls implementation including R1.9-R1.12 features)\n      - cmd/ls/ls_test.go (existing differential tests for R1.1-R1.8 -- follow the same test patterns)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary -- the differential testing API)\n      - CLAUDE.md (differential testing pattern and project conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/ls_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add DiffTest entries exercising srd008-ls R1.9 through R1.12\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Add DiffTest entries that exercise srd008-ls R1.9 per the SRD acceptance criteria -- each flag combination and edge case described in the SRD should have a test\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add DiffTest entries that exercise srd008-ls R1.10 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add DiffTest entries that exercise srd008-ls R1.11 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Add DiffTest entries that exercise srd008-ls R1.12 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Append new DiffTest entries to the existing tests slice in the TestDiff function -- do not create a separate test function\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Reference binary is gls from Homebrew via exec.LookPath(\\\"gls\\\"). If not found, the existing t.Skip call handles it -- do not add a second LookPath\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in the Env field of each DiffTest to ensure consistent sorting and locale behavior between Go and GNU binaries\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Create temporary directory fixtures for tests that need specific file layouts -- use t.TempDir() and populate with test files before running the diff test\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/ls/... -count=1 passes when gls is installed, or skips cleanly when gls is not found\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Each of R1.9, R1.10, R1.11, R1.12 has at least one DiffTest entry exercising its primary behavior\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Existing tests for R1.1-R1.8 continue to pass unchanged\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ls: remaining core and extended column layout (srd008-ls R1.13-R1.14, R2.1-R2.2)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml (requirements R1.13, R1.14, R2.1, R2.2 -- read full text and acceptance criteria)\n      - cmd/ls/main.go (existing ls implementation covering R1.1-R1.12 -- extend this file)\n      - pkg/sys/ (FileInfo, Stat, Lstat, TerminalWidth, IsTerminal -- may be needed for column layout)\n      - pkg/format/ (Columns, HumanSize, PadRight -- output formatting for column and extended display)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project build conventions and SIGPIPE handling requirement)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add implementation for srd008-ls requirements R1.13, R1.14, R2.1, R2.2\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R1.13 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R1.14 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R2.1 exactly as specified in the SRD -- this begins the extended feature set (R2 group)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls R2.2 exactly as specified in the SRD -- read the requirement text and acceptance criteria from the SRD file before coding\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/sys.TerminalWidth and pkg/sys.IsTerminal for terminal-aware column layout per architecture dependency srd008-ls -> srd002-sys\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/format.Columns for multi-column output per architecture dependency srd008-ls -> srd003-format. If pkg/format does not exist or is empty, implement column logic inline\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Extend existing flag parsing in cmd/ls/main.go -- add new flags to the existing flag set rather than creating a new parser\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Preserve all existing functionality from R1.1-R1.12 and the sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() call at the start of main\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ls builds successfully with go build -o bin/ls ./cmd/ls/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"srd008-ls requirements R1.13, R1.14, R2.1, and R2.2 are fully implemented as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/ls/... passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Existing functionality from R1.1-R1.12 is preserved -- no regressions\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ls: remaining core and extended column layout tests (srd008-ls R1.13-R1.14, R2.1-R2.2)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-require